---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with the Uinta Watch app — troubleshooting, permissions, and how to contact us. We're happy to help."
>
  <a href="#main-content" class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:bg-accent focus:text-ink rounded">Skip to content</a>
  <main id="main-content">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="section-loose bg-paper border-b border-paper-3">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-6">Support</p>
          <h1 class="text-display-xl text-ink mb-8">
            We're Here to<br/>
            <span class="text-accent">Help You Watch</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="text-ink-soft text-xl leading-relaxed">
            Answers to the most common questions, plus a direct line to the team behind
            Uinta Watch for the iOS app.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section bg-paper">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
          <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-6">
            <h2 class="text-display-lg text-ink mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Why does the app ask for my location?</h3>
              <p class="prose text-ink-soft text-sm">
                Uinta Watch requests location <em>only</em> when you use the <strong>Report</strong> feature, so your fire or
                smoke sighting can be tied to where you observed it. The sensor map never tracks your location. If you deny
                permission, the rest of the app still works — you just won't be able to attach a location to a report.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Why does the app ask for camera and photo access?</h3>
              <p class="prose text-ink-soft text-sm">
                So you can attach an optional photo to a report. The app only touches your camera or photo library when you
                explicitly choose an image, and never otherwise.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Do I need an account to use the app?</h3>
              <p class="prose text-ink-soft text-sm">
                No. Uinta Watch has no login, no sign-up, and no account system. Download it, open it, and everything works.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Does the app work without an internet connection?</h3>
              <p class="prose text-ink-soft text-sm">
                Yes. The current release ships with bundled sample sensor data, so the map, alerts, and sensor details all
                work fully offline. Live network data is on the way.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-2">How do I change app permissions?</h3>
              <p class="prose text-ink-soft text-sm">
                Open your device's <strong>Settings</strong>, scroll to <strong>Uinta Watch</strong>, and grant or revoke
                Location, Camera, or Photos access anytime.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-2">What is the app's data collection policy?</h3>
              <p class="prose text-ink-soft text-sm">
                We collect only what you submit through the Report feature. No ads, no analytics, no trackers. See our
                <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-dark underline">Privacy Policy</a> for full details.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Contact sidebar -->
          <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9">
            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-4">Contact Us</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft mb-4">
                Found a bug, have a feature request, or want to help build the network? Send us a note and we'll get back to you.
              </p>
              <a href="mailto:hello@uintawatch.com" class="btn-primary w-full justify-center">
                hello@uintawatch.com
              </a>
            </div>

            <div class="card mt-6">
              <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-ink mb-4">About the App</h3>
              <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                <div class="flex justify-between">
                  <span class="text-ink-muted">Version</span>
                  <span class="font-medium">1.0.0</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between">
                  <span class="text-ink-muted">Platform</span>
                  <span class="font-medium">iOS</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between">
                  <span class="text-ink-muted">Requires</span>
                  <span class="font-medium">iOS &amp; up</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex justify-between">
                  <span class="text-ink-muted">Cost</span>
                  <span class="font-medium">Free</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
